# Work logging (automatic, always)

This rule applies **every session** without exception. Logging is not optional and does not require user approval.

## Mandatory trigger

After completing **any substantive work**, append to `docs/engineering/WORK_LOG.md` as the **last implementation step** before your final response — even if the user did not mention documentation.

Substantive work includes: features, refactors, bug fixes, tests, config, behavioral docs, or plan completion.

Skip only for: pure Q&A, read-only exploration, or trivial typo fixes with zero behavioral impact.

## Procedure (do not skip)

1. Edit `docs/engineering/WORK_LOG.md`
2. Insert a new entry at the **top** of the Entries section (newest first)
3. Fill every template field (Status, Area, Summary, Key files, Tests, Related, Notes)
4. If a formal plan exists under `docs/superpowers/plans/`, update its checkboxes or link the completion record

## Rules

- **Never ask** whether to log — just log
- **Never defer** logging to a follow-up turn
- **Never omit** test/validation results when you ran them
- One log entry per coherent increment (split large multi-day work into logical entries)

## Entry quality

- **Summary**: outcome and why, not step-by-step narration
- **Key files**: real paths (created / modified / deleted)
- **Tests**: command run and pass/fail — exact counts when available
- **Related**: link completion record or authoritative doc updated
- **Notes**: follow-ups, known limits, deferred scope

## Also update when behavior changes

- Authoritative architecture/engineering doc (see [docs/README.md](docs/README.md))
- Plan checkboxes under `docs/superpowers/plans/` when formal plan exists
- [PROJECT_STATUS.md](docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md) for major milestones only
